    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d382">

                <pb facs="0572" n="458" sameAs="frus:frus1922v02/pg458"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">814.00/632: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Guatemala</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Curtis</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Guatemala</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-01-22T22:00:00-07:00"><hi rendition="#italic">January 22,
                                1922—10 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received January 23—8:50
                        p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>9. Convention of the Liberal Party this afternoon nominated Orellana.
                        Ubico<anchor n="2" xml:id="d382-f1"/> had previously pledged adherence to
                    the decision of the convention.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Curtis</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d382-f1" n="2" xml:id="d382-f1-content">
                <p>General Ubico, also, had been a candidate for the nomination.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
